### Earlier-study coverage and unique material

- [First jobs](../delvers/narrative/FIRST_JOBS.md): chapters 1–3 retain the main commissions and private context. The expanded pilot restores the S1E04 escape and second dungeon entry using its dossier; the older study ends during the earlier confrontation. Exact badge numbers, purchases, ceiling-warning details and provisional names remain in the study and dossiers rather than being discarded from the archive.
- [The Rise to Bronze](../delvers/narrative/THE_RISE_TO_BRONZE.md): chapter 4 retains temple discipline, Yuri's transfer, school's enchanted armor, Koh's finances, the hilt demonstration, warning, public service and naming. Shop-by-shop prices and unsettled commissions remain documented in its notes and S1E05.
- [Skull Keep](../delvers/narrative/SKULL_KEEP.md): chapter 5 retains research, client constraints, servants, first unsuccessful encounter, mechanism, motives, Enzo's attributed account and final victory. Puzzle input sequences and individual spell exchanges remain in the detailed study/dossier.
- [The Wells of Atomer](../delvers/narrative/THE_WELLS_OF_ATOMER.md): chapters 6–7 retain relationships, city/well investigation, temple discoveries, wife's contact, peace mission and lake outcomes. The pilot uses S1E08's distinction between Hall of Penance and main sanctuary, avoiding the older study's looser sanctuary wording. Detailed shopping, signal transliteration, gear placement and combat rounds remain accessible at their existing paths.

The older studies remain unchanged historical versions. Condensed tactical detail is reachable there and in dossiers; it is not rewritten into a competing current biography. All eight original numbered chapter headings and the unnumbered ending are retained in the pilot, preserving their anchors.

